<section class="prose app-templates" id="app-templates">
  <h2>Deploy them as app templates</h2>
  <p>
    Every stack in these guides is also in an app-template feed, so you can
    deploy it from your stack manager's template list and fill in the settings
    in a form:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{{ site.url }}/templates.json</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Portainer:</strong> Settings → App Templates → URL.</li>
    <li><strong>Dockhand:</strong> Templates → Sources → add the URL.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The feed lists {{ templates | length }} stacks:
    {% for t in templates %}<a href="/templates/{{ t.slug }}/docker-compose.yml">{{ t.slug }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
    Each one deploys the compose file from
    <a href="https://github.com/cubicecho/cubicecho.com/tree/main/templates" rel="noopener">this site's repo</a>,
    so you can also paste it into a new stack by hand.
  </p>
